=== layout: one-panel

# *Recombination Frequencies Do NOT Add!*

@body

- The b&#8211;vg recombination frequency (17%) is slightly less than the sum of the b&#8211;cn and cn&#8211;vg frequencies (9 + 9.5 = 18.5%).
  - This is because of the few times that crossover occurs between both b&#8211;cn and cn&#8211;vg.
  - A second crossover would "cancel out" the first, reducing the observed b&#8211;vg recombination frequency.
- The value of 18.5% (18.5 map units) is closer to the [*actual distance*]{underline=true} between the genes.
  - In practice, a geneticist would add the smaller distances in constructing a map.

